## Key Facts & Statistics (2025 Resale Report, GlobalData)
- The US secondhand apparel market grew 14% in 2024, 5x faster than the broader retail apparel market
- Online resale is projected to reach $40 billion in the US by 2029
- 68% of Gen Z and Millennials bought secondhand apparel in 2024
- The global secondhand market is projected to reach $350 billion by 2028
- thredUP processes items from 35,000+ brands
- Resale now accounts for 10% of US apparel market share, up from 7% in 2022
- New buyer growth on thredUP increased 95% in Q1 2025 vs. Q1 2024
- Surveyed 3,034 US consumers and 50 top fashion retail executives for the 2025 report

## How thredUP Works
- [Clean Out](https://www.thredup.com/cleanout): Send in a Clean Out Kit — thredUP processes, photographs, and lists items on your behalf
- [How Selling Works](https://www.thredup.com/how-it-works/selling): thredUP handles the entire selling process for consignors
- [How Buying Works](https://www.thredup.com/how-it-works/buying): Browse millions of items; all items are quality-checked before listing

## Sustainability
- thredUP estimates that buying one used item instead of new saves an average of 1.2 lbs of CO2
- The 2024 Impact Report documents carbon, water, and waste savings from thredUP transactions
- thredUP partners with major retailers on recommerce programs (e.g., resale-as-a-service)

## Platform Features
- AI-powered visual search: find items by uploading a photo
- Style Chat: AI styling assistant to discover items matching personal style preferences

